IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cbr-nouns`
IMPORT `cbr-reg1`
IMPORT `cbr-reg2-benefits`
IMPORT `cbr-reg2-couples`
IMPORT `cbr-reg2-rate`
IMPORT `cbr-reg3`

-- Child Benefit (Rates) Regulations 2006 (S.I. 2006/965) -- LAYER 2: THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a person who is responsible for a child or qualifying young person and claims
-- or receives Child Benefit, asking what weekly rate is payable for each child, and
-- when the enhanced rate is not paid for a second child (couples and polygamous
-- marriages).
--
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the cbr- modules imported above as
-- the questions that person asks. Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated:
-- each question builds the records the long modules expect, inside its WHERE, from
-- plain inputs, and calls the SAME module rule.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every input is a yes/no, a number, a date, or one of the modules'
-- own choices, one for each fact the person can state, and each `@desc` is worded as
-- that person would be asked. The facts are those at the START OF THE WEEK (reg 1(3)).
-- A record field that the rule called never reads is given a fixed placeholder, with a
-- comment saying so; fields a rule does read are always asked.
--
-- WHAT THE TEXT DOES NOT SAY (NOTES.md has the whole register): entitlement to child
-- benefit itself is out of this text (the parent Act is not encoded), so the
-- questions that need it ask first "is child benefit payable to me for this child?". Many questions
-- are therefore rate lookups. The other party's side of each relation is asked as
-- facts: the household members' circumstances (reg 2(2)(c)), the body that pays the
-- allowance (reg 2(5)), and the Commissioners' acceptance (reg 2(6)(c)(viii)).
--
-- THE TEXT PUTS NO DUTY OR LIABILITY ON THE PERSON: it does not require a claim, a
-- notice or a return, and imposes no penalty, so there is no "What do I owe?" question.
-- The only thing the person is exposed to is the Commissioners' judgment under reg
-- 2(6)(c)(viii), which is asked as an input.
--
-- NOT COVERED: the cases the rules return as NOTHING (see the result types).

§ `Child Benefit (Rates) Regulations 2006 -- the claimant's questions`

§§ `Regulation 1 -- whether these Regulations apply, and when the facts are tested`

-- Asked by anyone: the Regulations are worked out week by week (reg 1(3)).

-- reg 1(1). In force from 10 April 2006; a week is taken as in force if it begins on or after that day (fork F7).
@ref reg 1(1), commencement
@export Are these Regulations in force for the week I am asking about (reg 1(1))?
GIVEN `the first day of the week` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the week you are asking about? Child benefit is worked out a week at a time, and the facts that count are those at the start of that week. Give a date such as 2026-06-01.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are these Regulations in force for my week` IF
    `these Regulations are in force in the week beginning` `the first day of the week`

-- reg 1(2). One answer about Part 9 is given for both Acts; the rule reads only the Act that goes with where the young person is.
@ref reg 1(2) "qualifying young person"
@export Is the young person I look after a qualifying young person for these Regulations (reg 1(2))?
GIVEN `where the young person is` IS A `Where a young person is` @desc At the start of the week, where is the person you claim for: in Great Britain, in Northern Ireland, or in neither?
      `the young person is a qualifying young person under Part 9` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person you claim for a qualifying young person under Part 9 of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (if they are in Great Britain), or under Part 9 of the Northern Ireland Act of the same name (if they are in Northern Ireland)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the young person a qualifying young person` IF
    `a person is a qualifying young person for the purposes of these Regulations` `where the young person is` `the young person is a qualifying young person under Part 9` `the young person is a qualifying young person under Part 9`

-- reg 1(3). Every fact asked in this layer is the fact at the start of the week.
@ref reg 1(3)
@export On what day are the facts about me and my child tested for my week (reg 1(3))?
GIVEN `the first day of the week` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the week you are asking about? Child benefit is worked out a week at a time, and the facts that count are those at the start of that week. Give a date such as 2026-06-01.
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what day are the facts tested for my week` IS
    `the day on which conditions and facts are tested in the week beginning` `the first day of the week`

§§ `Regulation 2(1) -- the weekly rate for a child`

-- The headline questions. The form asks only the inputs that still matter: for example the payment questions only matter where regulation 2(4) bars the enhanced rate.

-- reg 2(1)-(5). NOTHING means the text does not cover the case: before the Regulations, before the version of the text encoded, not a child or qualifying young person, or two children born on the same day.
@ref reg 2(1), (2), (4), (5)
@export Does the enhanced rate or the rate in any other case apply to this child (reg 2(1))?
GIVEN `the first day of the week` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the week you are asking about? Child benefit is worked out a week at a time, and the facts that count are those at the start of that week. Give a date such as 2026-06-01.
      `child benefit is payable to me for this child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is child benefit payable to you for this child for the week? (Whether you are entitled to child benefit is decided by the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 and the Child Benefit (General) Regulations 2006, not by these Regulations.)
      `the child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is the child's date of birth?
      `the person I claim for is a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the start of the week, is the person you claim for a child for the purposes of child benefit?
      `where the young person is` IS A `Where a young person is` @desc At the start of the week, where is the person you claim for: in Great Britain, in Northern Ireland, or in neither?
      `the young person is a qualifying young person under Part 9` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person you claim for a qualifying young person under Part 9 of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (if they are in Great Britain), or under Part 9 of the Northern Ireland Act of the same name (if they are in Northern Ireland)?
      `this is the only or the eldest child I am paid child benefit for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this the only child, or the elder or eldest child, for whom child benefit is payable to you for the week?
      `I live with a parent of the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the start of the week, do you live with a parent of the child?
      `I live with that parent as mentioned in regulation 2(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you live with a parent of the child: is that as that parent's spouse or civil partner, as someone living with them as their spouse or civil partner, or as a fellow member of a polygamous marriage that you live in together? (Answer no if you do not live with a parent of the child.)
      `I am a voluntary organisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you claiming as a voluntary organisation, and not as an individual?
      `I live with my spouse or civil partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the start of the week, do you live with your spouse or civil partner?
      `I live with another person as my spouse or civil partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the start of the week, do you live with another person as if they were your spouse or civil partner?
      `a party to my marriage is married to more than one person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc While your marriage lasts, is any party to it married to more than one person? (Answer no if you are not married.)
      `my marriage ceremony took place under the law of a country which permits polygamy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the ceremony of your marriage take place under the law of a country which permits polygamy? (Answer no if you are not married.)
      `I live with the other members of my marriage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the start of the week, do you live with the other members of that marriage? (Answer no if you are not in a polygamous marriage.)
      `child benefit would be payable at the enhanced rate to someone else in my household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Apart from the rule for couples and polygamous marriages, would child benefit be payable at the enhanced rate for another child to your spouse, civil partner, the person you live with as a couple, or another member of your polygamous marriage?
      `the date of birth of the eldest of the children they would be paid the enhanced rate for` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the date of birth of the elder or eldest of the children for whom child benefit would be payable to them at the enhanced rate? (Give any date if you answered no.)
      `the kind of payment I am paid for the week` IS A `Kind of payment made for the week` @desc What kind of payment are you paid for the week, as an allowance or an increase of a benefit, pension or allowance?
      `receiving it entitles me to an increase for dependants listed in Schedule 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a benefit under one of the two Acts: does receiving it entitle you to an increase for dependants of the kind listed in the Table in Schedule 4 to that Act?
      `the instrument the allowance is granted under` IS AN `Instrument granting an allowance for a child on a death due to service or war injury` @desc If it is an allowance for a child on a death due to service or war injury: which instrument grants it, or is it none of the listed ones?
      `the Commissioners accept it as analogous to a listed allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is an allowance for a child on a death due to service or war injury under none of the listed instruments: have the Commissioners for Revenue and Customs accepted it as analogous to one that is?
      `the payment is paid to me for the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that payment paid to you in respect of the week?
      `the payment is paid for this child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that payment paid in respect of this child?
GIVETH A MAYBE `Case under regulation 2(1)`
DECIDE `Which case under regulation 2(1) applies to this child` IS
    `the case under regulation 2(1) for the child in the week beginning` `the first day of the week` `my circumstances` `this child` `my payment` `the others in my household`
    WHERE
        `my circumstances` MEANS `Claimant at the start of the week` WITH
            `a voluntary organisation` IS `I am a voluntary organisation`
            `living with the claimant's spouse or civil partner` IS `I live with my spouse or civil partner`
            `living with another person as the claimant's spouse or civil partner` IS `I live with another person as my spouse or civil partner`
            `during the marriage a party to it is married to more than one person` IS `a party to my marriage is married to more than one person`
            `the ceremony of the marriage took place under the law of a country which permits polygamy` IS `my marriage ceremony took place under the law of a country which permits polygamy`
            `residing with other members of that marriage` IS `I live with the other members of my marriage`
        `this child` MEANS `Child or qualifying young person at the start of the week` WITH
            `date of birth` IS `the child's date of birth`
            `child benefit is payable to the claimant in respect of the child or qualifying young person` IS `child benefit is payable to me for this child`
            `a child for the purposes of child benefit` IS `the person I claim for is a child`
            `where the young person is` IS `where the young person is`
            `a qualifying young person for the purposes of Part 9 of SSCBA` IS `the young person is a qualifying young person under Part 9`
            `a qualifying young person for the purposes of Part 9 of SSCB(NI)A` IS `the young person is a qualifying young person under Part 9`
            `the only person, or the elder or eldest person, in respect of whom child benefit is payable to the claimant` IS `this is the only or the eldest child I am paid child benefit for`
            `the claimant resides with a parent of the child or qualifying young person` IS `I live with a parent of the child`
            `the claimant resides with that parent as mentioned in paragraph (2)(a)` IS `I live with that parent as mentioned in regulation 2(2)(a)`
        `my payment` MEANS `Payment made for the week` WITH
            `kind of payment` IS `the kind of payment I am paid for the week`
            `receipt of the benefit entitles the recipient to an increase for dependants specified in the Table in Schedule 4 to that Act` IS `receiving it entitles me to an increase for dependants listed in Schedule 4`
            `instrument granting the allowance` IS `the instrument the allowance is granted under`
            `the Commissioners accept the allowance as analogous to one granted under those instruments` IS `the Commissioners accept it as analogous to a listed allowance`
            `paid to the claimant in respect of the week` IS `the payment is paid to me for the week`
            `paid in respect of the child or qualifying young person` IS `the payment is paid for this child`
        `the others in my household` MEANS `Other persons listed in paragraph (2)(a) at the start of the week` WITH
            `child benefit would, but for paragraph (2), be payable at the enhanced rate to one of them for another child or qualifying person` IS `child benefit would be payable at the enhanced rate to someone else in my household`
            `date of birth of the elder or eldest of those other children` IS `the date of birth of the eldest of the children they would be paid the enhanced rate for`

-- reg 2(1) and reg 3(1). NOTHING means the text does not cover the case (see the question above). The saving is out of text: the amount the earlier rates would have given is asked as a plain input.
@ref reg 2(1)-(5), reg 3
@export What weekly amount of child benefit is payable for this child, in pounds (reg 2 and reg 3)?
GIVEN `the first day of the week` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the week you are asking about? Child benefit is worked out a week at a time, and the facts that count are those at the start of that week. Give a date such as 2026-06-01.
      `child benefit is payable to me for this child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is child benefit payable to you for this child for the week? (Whether you are entitled to child benefit is decided by the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 and the Child Benefit (General) Regulations 2006, not by these Regulations.)
      `the child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is the child's date of birth?
      `the person I claim for is a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the start of the week, is the person you claim for a child for the purposes of child benefit?
      `where the young person is` IS A `Where a young person is` @desc At the start of the week, where is the person you claim for: in Great Britain, in Northern Ireland, or in neither?
      `the young person is a qualifying young person under Part 9` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person you claim for a qualifying young person under Part 9 of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (if they are in Great Britain), or under Part 9 of the Northern Ireland Act of the same name (if they are in Northern Ireland)?
      `this is the only or the eldest child I am paid child benefit for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this the only child, or the elder or eldest child, for whom child benefit is payable to you for the week?
      `I live with a parent of the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the start of the week, do you live with a parent of the child?
      `I live with that parent as mentioned in regulation 2(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you live with a parent of the child: is that as that parent's spouse or civil partner, as someone living with them as their spouse or civil partner, or as a fellow member of a polygamous marriage that you live in together? (Answer no if you do not live with a parent of the child.)
      `I am a voluntary organisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you claiming as a voluntary organisation, and not as an individual?
      `I live with my spouse or civil partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the start of the week, do you live with your spouse or civil partner?
      `I live with another person as my spouse or civil partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the start of the week, do you live with another person as if they were your spouse or civil partner?
      `a party to my marriage is married to more than one person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc While your marriage lasts, is any party to it married to more than one person? (Answer no if you are not married.)
      `my marriage ceremony took place under the law of a country which permits polygamy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the ceremony of your marriage take place under the law of a country which permits polygamy? (Answer no if you are not married.)
      `I live with the other members of my marriage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the start of the week, do you live with the other members of that marriage? (Answer no if you are not in a polygamous marriage.)
      `child benefit would be payable at the enhanced rate to someone else in my household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Apart from the rule for couples and polygamous marriages, would child benefit be payable at the enhanced rate for another child to your spouse, civil partner, the person you live with as a couple, or another member of your polygamous marriage?
      `the date of birth of the eldest of the children they would be paid the enhanced rate for` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the date of birth of the elder or eldest of the children for whom child benefit would be payable to them at the enhanced rate? (Give any date if you answered no.)
      `the kind of payment I am paid for the week` IS A `Kind of payment made for the week` @desc What kind of payment are you paid for the week, as an allowance or an increase of a benefit, pension or allowance?
      `receiving it entitles me to an increase for dependants listed in Schedule 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a benefit under one of the two Acts: does receiving it entitle you to an increase for dependants of the kind listed in the Table in Schedule 4 to that Act?
      `the instrument the allowance is granted under` IS AN `Instrument granting an allowance for a child on a death due to service or war injury` @desc If it is an allowance for a child on a death due to service or war injury: which instrument grants it, or is it none of the listed ones?
      `the Commissioners accept it as analogous to a listed allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is an allowance for a child on a death due to service or war injury under none of the listed instruments: have the Commissioners for Revenue and Customs accepted it as analogous to one that is?
      `the payment is paid to me for the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that payment paid to you in respect of the week?
      `the payment is paid for this child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that payment paid in respect of this child?
      `the earlier rates with the 1998 savings would have given me an amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the earlier 1976 child benefit rates, with the transitional provisions and savings of the 1998 amendment regulations, have given you an amount for this child for the week?
      `the weekly amount the earlier rates would have given me` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how much a week, in pounds, would they have given you? (Give 0 if you answered no.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What weekly amount of child benefit is payable for this child` IS
    `the weekly amount payable after the saving in regulation 3` (`the weekly rate of child benefit under regulation 2 for the child in the week beginning` `the first day of the week` `my circumstances` `this child` `my payment` `the others in my household`) `the amount the earlier rates would give me`
    WHERE
        `my circumstances` MEANS `Claimant at the start of the week` WITH
            `a voluntary organisation` IS `I am a voluntary organisation`
            `living with the claimant's spouse or civil partner` IS `I live with my spouse or civil partner`
            `living with another person as the claimant's spouse or civil partner` IS `I live with another person as my spouse or civil partner`
            `during the marriage a party to it is married to more than one person` IS `a party to my marriage is married to more than one person`
            `the ceremony of the marriage took place under the law of a country which permits polygamy` IS `my marriage ceremony took place under the law of a country which permits polygamy`
            `residing with other members of that marriage` IS `I live with the other members of my marriage`
        `this child` MEANS `Child or qualifying young person at the start of the week` WITH
            `date of birth` IS `the child's date of birth`
            `child benefit is payable to the claimant in respect of the child or qualifying young person` IS `child benefit is payable to me for this child`
            `a child for the purposes of child benefit` IS `the person I claim for is a child`
            `where the young person is` IS `where the young person is`
            `a qualifying young person for the purposes of Part 9 of SSCBA` IS `the young person is a qualifying young person under Part 9`
            `a qualifying young person for the purposes of Part 9 of SSCB(NI)A` IS `the young person is a qualifying young person under Part 9`
            `the only person, or the elder or eldest person, in respect of whom child benefit is payable to the claimant` IS `this is the only or the eldest child I am paid child benefit for`
            `the claimant resides with a parent of the child or qualifying young person` IS `I live with a parent of the child`
            `the claimant resides with that parent as mentioned in paragraph (2)(a)` IS `I live with that parent as mentioned in regulation 2(2)(a)`
        `my payment` MEANS `Payment made for the week` WITH
            `kind of payment` IS `the kind of payment I am paid for the week`
            `receipt of the benefit entitles the recipient to an increase for dependants specified in the Table in Schedule 4 to that Act` IS `receiving it entitles me to an increase for dependants listed in Schedule 4`
            `instrument granting the allowance` IS `the instrument the allowance is granted under`
            `the Commissioners accept the allowance as analogous to one granted under those instruments` IS `the Commissioners accept it as analogous to a listed allowance`
            `paid to the claimant in respect of the week` IS `the payment is paid to me for the week`
            `paid in respect of the child or qualifying young person` IS `the payment is paid for this child`
        `the others in my household` MEANS `Other persons listed in paragraph (2)(a) at the start of the week` WITH
            `child benefit would, but for paragraph (2), be payable at the enhanced rate to one of them for another child or qualifying person` IS `child benefit would be payable at the enhanced rate to someone else in my household`
            `date of birth of the elder or eldest of those other children` IS `the date of birth of the eldest of the children they would be paid the enhanced rate for`
        `the amount the earlier rates would give me` MEANS
            IF `the earlier rates with the 1998 savings would have given me an amount`
            THEN JUST `the weekly amount the earlier rates would have given me`
            ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Regulation 2(2) and (3) -- couples and polygamous marriages`

-- Only for someone who lives with a spouse, civil partner or partner, or in a polygamous marriage. A form can ask "Do you live with a spouse, civil partner or partner, or in a polygamous marriage?" before showing this group.

-- reg 2(2)(a)(i) to (iii).
@ref reg 2(2)(a)
@export Am I in a household where the couples rule in regulation 2(2) can apply to me (reg 2(2)(a))?
GIVEN `I live with my spouse or civil partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the start of the week, do you live with your spouse or civil partner?
      `I live with another person as my spouse or civil partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the start of the week, do you live with another person as if they were your spouse or civil partner?
      `a party to my marriage is married to more than one person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc While your marriage lasts, is any party to it married to more than one person? (Answer no if you are not married.)
      `my marriage ceremony took place under the law of a country which permits polygamy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the ceremony of your marriage take place under the law of a country which permits polygamy? (Answer no if you are not married.)
      `I live with the other members of my marriage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the start of the week, do you live with the other members of that marriage? (Answer no if you are not in a polygamous marriage.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the couples rule apply to me` IF
    `paragraph (2)(a) applies to the claimant` `my circumstances`
    WHERE
        `my circumstances` MEANS `Claimant at the start of the week` WITH
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `a voluntary organisation` IS FALSE
            `living with the claimant's spouse or civil partner` IS `I live with my spouse or civil partner`
            `living with another person as the claimant's spouse or civil partner` IS `I live with another person as my spouse or civil partner`
            `during the marriage a party to it is married to more than one person` IS `a party to my marriage is married to more than one person`
            `the ceremony of the marriage took place under the law of a country which permits polygamy` IS `my marriage ceremony took place under the law of a country which permits polygamy`
            `residing with other members of that marriage` IS `I live with the other members of my marriage`

-- reg 2(3): both (a) and (b).
@ref reg 2(3)
@export Am I a member of a polygamous marriage (reg 2(3))?
GIVEN `a party to my marriage is married to more than one person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc While your marriage lasts, is any party to it married to more than one person? (Answer no if you are not married.)
      `my marriage ceremony took place under the law of a country which permits polygamy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the ceremony of your marriage take place under the law of a country which permits polygamy? (Answer no if you are not married.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a member of a polygamous marriage` IF
    `a claimant is a member of a polygamous marriage` `my circumstances`
    WHERE
        `my circumstances` MEANS `Claimant at the start of the week` WITH
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `a voluntary organisation` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `living with the claimant's spouse or civil partner` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `living with another person as the claimant's spouse or civil partner` IS FALSE
            `during the marriage a party to it is married to more than one person` IS `a party to my marriage is married to more than one person`
            `the ceremony of the marriage took place under the law of a country which permits polygamy` IS `my marriage ceremony took place under the law of a country which permits polygamy`
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `residing with other members of that marriage` IS FALSE

-- reg 2(2). JUST TRUE: the enhanced rate stays with this child. JUST FALSE: it is paid for only an older child of someone else in the household. NOTHING: the two children were born on the same day and the text does not say which is the elder (fork F3).
@ref reg 2(2)
@export Is the enhanced rate paid for my child, or only for an older child in my household (reg 2(2))?
GIVEN `child benefit is payable to me for this child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is child benefit payable to you for this child for the week? (Whether you are entitled to child benefit is decided by the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 and the Child Benefit (General) Regulations 2006, not by these Regulations.)
      `the child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is the child's date of birth?
      `this is the only or the eldest child I am paid child benefit for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this the only child, or the elder or eldest child, for whom child benefit is payable to you for the week?
      `I live with a parent of the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the start of the week, do you live with a parent of the child?
      `I live with that parent as mentioned in regulation 2(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you live with a parent of the child: is that as that parent's spouse or civil partner, as someone living with them as their spouse or civil partner, or as a fellow member of a polygamous marriage that you live in together? (Answer no if you do not live with a parent of the child.)
      `I am a voluntary organisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you claiming as a voluntary organisation, and not as an individual?
      `I live with my spouse or civil partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the start of the week, do you live with your spouse or civil partner?
      `I live with another person as my spouse or civil partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the start of the week, do you live with another person as if they were your spouse or civil partner?
      `a party to my marriage is married to more than one person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc While your marriage lasts, is any party to it married to more than one person? (Answer no if you are not married.)
      `my marriage ceremony took place under the law of a country which permits polygamy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the ceremony of your marriage take place under the law of a country which permits polygamy? (Answer no if you are not married.)
      `I live with the other members of my marriage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the start of the week, do you live with the other members of that marriage? (Answer no if you are not in a polygamous marriage.)
      `child benefit would be payable at the enhanced rate to someone else in my household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Apart from the rule for couples and polygamous marriages, would child benefit be payable at the enhanced rate for another child to your spouse, civil partner, the person you live with as a couple, or another member of your polygamous marriage?
      `the date of birth of the eldest of the children they would be paid the enhanced rate for` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the date of birth of the elder or eldest of the children for whom child benefit would be payable to them at the enhanced rate? (Give any date if you answered no.)
      `the kind of payment I am paid for the week` IS A `Kind of payment made for the week` @desc What kind of payment are you paid for the week, as an allowance or an increase of a benefit, pension or allowance?
      `receiving it entitles me to an increase for dependants listed in Schedule 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a benefit under one of the two Acts: does receiving it entitle you to an increase for dependants of the kind listed in the Table in Schedule 4 to that Act?
      `the instrument the allowance is granted under` IS AN `Instrument granting an allowance for a child on a death due to service or war injury` @desc If it is an allowance for a child on a death due to service or war injury: which instrument grants it, or is it none of the listed ones?
      `the Commissioners accept it as analogous to a listed allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is an allowance for a child on a death due to service or war injury under none of the listed instruments: have the Commissioners for Revenue and Customs accepted it as analogous to one that is?
      `the payment is paid to me for the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that payment paid to you in respect of the week?
      `the payment is paid for this child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that payment paid in respect of this child?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the enhanced rate paid for my child under the couples rule` IS
    `paragraph (2) allows the enhanced rate for the claimant's child` `my circumstances` (`this child`'s `date of birth`) (`the enhanced rate would, but for paragraph (2), be payable for the child` `my circumstances` `this child` `my payment`) `the others in my household`
    WHERE
        `my circumstances` MEANS `Claimant at the start of the week` WITH
            `a voluntary organisation` IS `I am a voluntary organisation`
            `living with the claimant's spouse or civil partner` IS `I live with my spouse or civil partner`
            `living with another person as the claimant's spouse or civil partner` IS `I live with another person as my spouse or civil partner`
            `during the marriage a party to it is married to more than one person` IS `a party to my marriage is married to more than one person`
            `the ceremony of the marriage took place under the law of a country which permits polygamy` IS `my marriage ceremony took place under the law of a country which permits polygamy`
            `residing with other members of that marriage` IS `I live with the other members of my marriage`
        `this child` MEANS `Child or qualifying young person at the start of the week` WITH
            `date of birth` IS `the child's date of birth`
            `child benefit is payable to the claimant in respect of the child or qualifying young person` IS `child benefit is payable to me for this child`
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `a child for the purposes of child benefit` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `where the young person is` IS `in Great Britain`
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `a qualifying young person for the purposes of Part 9 of SSCBA` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `a qualifying young person for the purposes of Part 9 of SSCB(NI)A` IS FALSE
            `the only person, or the elder or eldest person, in respect of whom child benefit is payable to the claimant` IS `this is the only or the eldest child I am paid child benefit for`
            `the claimant resides with a parent of the child or qualifying young person` IS `I live with a parent of the child`
            `the claimant resides with that parent as mentioned in paragraph (2)(a)` IS `I live with that parent as mentioned in regulation 2(2)(a)`
        `my payment` MEANS `Payment made for the week` WITH
            `kind of payment` IS `the kind of payment I am paid for the week`
            `receipt of the benefit entitles the recipient to an increase for dependants specified in the Table in Schedule 4 to that Act` IS `receiving it entitles me to an increase for dependants listed in Schedule 4`
            `instrument granting the allowance` IS `the instrument the allowance is granted under`
            `the Commissioners accept the allowance as analogous to one granted under those instruments` IS `the Commissioners accept it as analogous to a listed allowance`
            `paid to the claimant in respect of the week` IS `the payment is paid to me for the week`
            `paid in respect of the child or qualifying young person` IS `the payment is paid for this child`
        `the others in my household` MEANS `Other persons listed in paragraph (2)(a) at the start of the week` WITH
            `child benefit would, but for paragraph (2), be payable at the enhanced rate to one of them for another child or qualifying person` IS `child benefit would be payable at the enhanced rate to someone else in my household`
            `date of birth of the elder or eldest of those other children` IS `the date of birth of the eldest of the children they would be paid the enhanced rate for`

§§ `Regulation 2(4) -- when the enhanced rate is not paid`

-- Applies to everyone: only a voluntary organisation, or someone living with a parent of the child otherwise than as a couple, is caught.

-- reg 2(4)(a) and (b). A later paragraph, (5), can give the enhanced rate back (fork F1).
@ref reg 2(4)
@export Is the enhanced rate withheld from this child because I am a voluntary organisation or live with the child's parent (reg 2(4))?
GIVEN `I am a voluntary organisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you claiming as a voluntary organisation, and not as an individual?
      `I live with a parent of the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the start of the week, do you live with a parent of the child?
      `I live with that parent as mentioned in regulation 2(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you live with a parent of the child: is that as that parent's spouse or civil partner, as someone living with them as their spouse or civil partner, or as a fellow member of a polygamous marriage that you live in together? (Answer no if you do not live with a parent of the child.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the enhanced rate withheld from this child by regulation 2(4)` IF
    `paragraph (4) bars the enhanced rate` `my circumstances` `this child`
    WHERE
        `my circumstances` MEANS `Claimant at the start of the week` WITH
            `a voluntary organisation` IS `I am a voluntary organisation`
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `living with the claimant's spouse or civil partner` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `living with another person as the claimant's spouse or civil partner` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `during the marriage a party to it is married to more than one person` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the ceremony of the marriage took place under the law of a country which permits polygamy` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `residing with other members of that marriage` IS FALSE
        `this child` MEANS `Child or qualifying young person at the start of the week` WITH
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 2000
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `child benefit is payable to the claimant in respect of the child or qualifying young person` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `a child for the purposes of child benefit` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `where the young person is` IS `in Great Britain`
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `a qualifying young person for the purposes of Part 9 of SSCBA` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `a qualifying young person for the purposes of Part 9 of SSCB(NI)A` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the only person, or the elder or eldest person, in respect of whom child benefit is payable to the claimant` IS FALSE
            `the claimant resides with a parent of the child or qualifying young person` IS `I live with a parent of the child`
            `the claimant resides with that parent as mentioned in paragraph (2)(a)` IS `I live with that parent as mentioned in regulation 2(2)(a)`

§§ `Regulation 2(5) and (6) -- benefits that give the enhanced rate`

-- Only for someone who is paid an allowance, or an increase of a benefit, pension or allowance, for the week. A form can ask "Are you paid an allowance or an increase of a benefit for a child?" before showing this group.

-- reg 2(6)(a), (b), (c)(i) to (vii) and (c)(viii). Whether the Commissioners accept an allowance as analogous is their judgment, so it is asked, not guessed.
@ref reg 2(6)
@export Is the payment I receive a specified benefit (reg 2(6))?
GIVEN `the kind of payment I am paid for the week` IS A `Kind of payment made for the week` @desc What kind of payment are you paid for the week, as an allowance or an increase of a benefit, pension or allowance?
      `receiving it entitles me to an increase for dependants listed in Schedule 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a benefit under one of the two Acts: does receiving it entitle you to an increase for dependants of the kind listed in the Table in Schedule 4 to that Act?
      `the instrument the allowance is granted under` IS AN `Instrument granting an allowance for a child on a death due to service or war injury` @desc If it is an allowance for a child on a death due to service or war injury: which instrument grants it, or is it none of the listed ones?
      `the Commissioners accept it as analogous to a listed allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is an allowance for a child on a death due to service or war injury under none of the listed instruments: have the Commissioners for Revenue and Customs accepted it as analogous to one that is?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my payment a specified benefit` IF
    `a payment is a specified benefit` `my payment`
    WHERE
        `my payment` MEANS `Payment made for the week` WITH
            `kind of payment` IS `the kind of payment I am paid for the week`
            `receipt of the benefit entitles the recipient to an increase for dependants specified in the Table in Schedule 4 to that Act` IS `receiving it entitles me to an increase for dependants listed in Schedule 4`
            `instrument granting the allowance` IS `the instrument the allowance is granted under`
            `the Commissioners accept the allowance as analogous to one granted under those instruments` IS `the Commissioners accept it as analogous to a listed allowance`
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `paid to the claimant in respect of the week` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `paid in respect of the child or qualifying young person` IS FALSE

-- reg 2(5)(a) and (b).
@ref reg 2(5)
@export Does the payment I receive give me the enhanced rate for this child (reg 2(5))?
GIVEN `this is the only or the eldest child I am paid child benefit for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this the only child, or the elder or eldest child, for whom child benefit is payable to you for the week?
      `the kind of payment I am paid for the week` IS A `Kind of payment made for the week` @desc What kind of payment are you paid for the week, as an allowance or an increase of a benefit, pension or allowance?
      `receiving it entitles me to an increase for dependants listed in Schedule 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a benefit under one of the two Acts: does receiving it entitle you to an increase for dependants of the kind listed in the Table in Schedule 4 to that Act?
      `the instrument the allowance is granted under` IS AN `Instrument granting an allowance for a child on a death due to service or war injury` @desc If it is an allowance for a child on a death due to service or war injury: which instrument grants it, or is it none of the listed ones?
      `the Commissioners accept it as analogous to a listed allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is an allowance for a child on a death due to service or war injury under none of the listed instruments: have the Commissioners for Revenue and Customs accepted it as analogous to one that is?
      `the payment is paid to me for the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that payment paid to you in respect of the week?
      `the payment is paid for this child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that payment paid in respect of this child?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my payment give me the enhanced rate for this child` IF
    `paragraph (5) gives the enhanced rate for the child` `my payment` `this child`
    WHERE
        `this child` MEANS `Child or qualifying young person at the start of the week` WITH
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 2000
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `child benefit is payable to the claimant in respect of the child or qualifying young person` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `a child for the purposes of child benefit` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `where the young person is` IS `in Great Britain`
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `a qualifying young person for the purposes of Part 9 of SSCBA` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `a qualifying young person for the purposes of Part 9 of SSCB(NI)A` IS FALSE
            `the only person, or the elder or eldest person, in respect of whom child benefit is payable to the claimant` IS `this is the only or the eldest child I am paid child benefit for`
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the claimant resides with a parent of the child or qualifying young person` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the claimant resides with that parent as mentioned in paragraph (2)(a)` IS FALSE
        `my payment` MEANS `Payment made for the week` WITH
            `kind of payment` IS `the kind of payment I am paid for the week`
            `receipt of the benefit entitles the recipient to an increase for dependants specified in the Table in Schedule 4 to that Act` IS `receiving it entitles me to an increase for dependants listed in Schedule 4`
            `instrument granting the allowance` IS `the instrument the allowance is granted under`
            `the Commissioners accept the allowance as analogous to one granted under those instruments` IS `the Commissioners accept it as analogous to a listed allowance`
            `paid to the claimant in respect of the week` IS `the payment is paid to me for the week`
            `paid in respect of the child or qualifying young person` IS `the payment is paid for this child`

§§ `Regulation 3 -- the saving of the earlier rates`

-- Only for someone whose child benefit was fixed under the 1976 Regulations before they were revoked, with a transitional provision or saving in the 1998 amendment regulations. A form can ask "Was your child benefit already being paid before these Regulations?" before showing this group.

-- reg 3(2)(a) and (b).
@ref reg 3(2)
@export Which transitional provisions and savings decide whether the earlier rates give me more (reg 3(2))?
GIVEN `the Act under which my child benefit is payable` IS AN `Act under which child benefit is payable` @desc Is your child benefit payable under the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (Great Britain) or the Northern Ireland Act of the same name?
GIVETH A `Transitional provisions and savings in regulation 3(2)`
DECIDE `Which transitional provisions and savings apply to me` IS
    `the relevant transitional provisions and savings for` `the Act under which my child benefit is payable`

-- reg 3(1). The amount the earlier rates would have given is out of text, so it is asked.
@ref reg 3(1)
@export How much am I paid, in pounds a week, if the earlier rates would have given me more (reg 3(1))?
GIVEN `the weekly amount these Regulations prescribe for this child` IS A NUMBER @desc What weekly amount, in pounds, do these Regulations prescribe for this child? (Answer the question on the weekly rate first.)
      `the earlier rates with the 1998 savings would have given me an amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the earlier 1976 child benefit rates, with the transitional provisions and savings of the 1998 amendment regulations, have given you an amount for this child for the week?
      `the weekly amount the earlier rates would have given me` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how much a week, in pounds, would they have given you? (Give 0 if you answered no.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the greater amount payable under the saving` IS
    `the greater amount payable under regulation 3(1)` `the weekly amount these Regulations prescribe for this child` `the amount the earlier rates would give me`
    WHERE
        `the amount the earlier rates would give me` MEANS
            IF `the earlier rates with the 1998 savings would have given me an amount`
            THEN JUST `the weekly amount the earlier rates would have given me`
            ELSE NOTHING
